ame><surname>de Backer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><source>Maten en Gewichten. Handleiding voor gestandaardiseerde kwantificering van voedingsmiddelen in Belgi&#x000eb;, revisie januari 2005</source><publisher-name>Hoge Gezondheidsraad, Ministerie van Sociale Zaken, Volksgezondheid en Leefmilieu</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Brussels, Belgium</publisher-loc><year>2005</year></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ijerph-06-00382"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holland</surname><given-names>NT</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Eskenazi</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bastaki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biological sample collection and processing for molecular epidemiological studies</article-title><source>Mutat. Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>543</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>234</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12787814</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21-ijerph-06-00382"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wessels</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Barr</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mendola</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of biomarkers to indicate exposure of children to organophosphate pesticides: implications for a longitudinal study of children&#x02019;s environmental health</article-title><source>Environ. Health Perspect</source><year>2003</year><volume>111</volume><fpage>1939</fpage><lpage>1946</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14644670</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22-ijerph-06-00382"><label>22.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shahar</surname><given-names>D</given-names></nam